DEVICE=A:\HIMEM.SYS
DOS=HIGH,UMB
FILES=20
BUFFERS=20
LASTDRIVE=E
REM HIMEM.SYS + DOS=HIGH free conventional memory so the 386+ HWiNFO build
REM fits under 640K. On a true 8088 there is no HMA: HIMEM just skips (it
REM prints "requires an 80286" and continues) and DOS=HIGH is ignored -- both
REM harmless. MSD needs no XMS, so the 8088/286 path is unaffected.
